# s4_onnx_single_export (second measurement of this mechanism; re-derived order, 2026-08-04; off-path)
#
# basis      s3_trace_nograd peak 2482984 kB; Beaver hump ~2.48 GB, binding instant = model conversion:
#   heap:python3.10+0x13cc27         867.0 MB  0.341   <- this step (the io.BytesIO export buffer)
#   heap:libstdc++.so+0xf4979        867.0 MB  0.341   <- same object's serializer-side twin
#   heap:libc10.so+0x4a675           433.0 MB  0.170   (the model tensors at conversion)
#   anon:[heap]                      130.0 MB  0.051
# object     in-memory ONNX buffer (867 MB for 433 MB, io.BytesIO doubling), held twice (Python buffer,
#            serializer copy). Fix: export once to a node-local file, convert from the file.
# history    file-export alone (retired off-path/s5_onnx_file_export): -4.1%, +3.4% wall (paid); single
#            export: free. Exported graph byte-identical; draws untouched.
# skips      none at this instant; parameter set and Beaver operand groups are on the other hump
#            (dispositions from s2/s3).
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: python3.10+0x13cc27
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu
